					"patching_rect" : [ 20.408163070678711, 83.673468589782715, 391.216222167015076, 167.0 ],
					"text" : "Modifying a video for sonification requires specific video processing to create a resampled and simplified image for the clean generation of sound. (Otherwise you get constant noise and it's not very interesting)\n\nHere I take a webcam input, downsample the resolution, convert it to black and white, create a threshold, and a filter to create a trail effect. The result of the video processing is then sampled by a single pixel \"slice\", which is then mapped onto an oscillator.\n\nThe global controls at the top make the patch easy to use by pulling out a few editable paramters that change the nature of the visualization and sound."
				}

